---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Booking software for community pottery studios"
	description="Booking software for community and membership pottery studios: shared kiln queues, wheel time reservations by membership tier, open-studio check-in and classes in one place."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">For community studios</p>
				<h1>One studio, a hundred members, three kilns.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Community and membership studios share everything: the kilns, the wheels, the good glaze
					shelf. Kilnbook keeps track of who has what booked, what is in which load, and who is in
					the building during open studio.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/studio-floor.svg"
				alt="A community studio floor with a row of wheels, hand-building tables and a kiln room"
				width="560"
				height="360"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</p>
			<h2>What gets hard when members share a studio</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>The kiln log lives on a clipboard</h3>
					<p>
						Pieces pile up on the bisque shelf with no name on them, firing fees get counted by hand
						at the end of the month, and members keep asking if their bowl is out yet.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Everyone wants Thursday at 6pm</h3>
					<p>
						The sign-up sheet by the door fills in minutes, a few members book every evening, and
						nobody knows who actually turned up.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Classes and members collide</h3>
					<p>
						A Saturday course takes over half the wheels, members show up for open studio anyway,
						and class credits are tracked in a spreadsheet only one person understands.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Shared kilns, one queue each</h2>
		<p>
			Members log a piece from their phone when they set it on the shelf. Kilnbook charges the firing
			fee by cubic inch or per piece, adds it to the right bisque or glaze load for that kiln, and
			texts every member with work in the load when it is ready for pickup. Your firing log fills
			itself in as you go.
			<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Wheel time that is fair to every member</h2>
		<p>
			Members reserve wheels, hand-building tables and shared equipment in one-hour blocks. Set how
			many hours each membership tier gets a week and how far ahead they can book, make evenings and
			weekends count double, and decide what a no-show costs. Cancelled slots go back on the calendar
			right away.
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">Wheel and table booking</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Open-studio hours you can see</h2>
		<p>
			Put a tablet by the door for open studio. Members tap their name when they arrive, so you always
			know who is in the building, which matters when the kilns are running and nobody from staff is
			on the floor.
		</p>

		<h2>Classes alongside membership</h2>
		<p>
			Run six-week courses, drop-ins and class packs from the same calendar your members book from,
			so a Saturday class and open studio never fight over the same wheels. Waitlists fill cancelled
			seats by text, and instructors see their roster on the studio tablet.
			<a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan fits a community studio?</h2>
		<p>
			Most community studios run on the Studio plan: $79 a month for up to 3 kilns and unlimited
			members, with wheel and table reservations, class packs, waitlists, memberships and pickup
			texts included. Add a fourth kiln or a second location and the Collective plan covers unlimited
			kilns. <a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Give your members the studio calendar.</h2>
			<p>30 days free on the Studio plan. No card to start, and nothing is deleted if you walk away.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
